{
  "scene": {
    "id": "check-pilot4",
    "language": "[0]All right, so I'm going to be explaining checking. So again, our goal is to take the ball to the goal to score. And right now, when the opponent is right in front of[1] me, that is not... Okay. That is not going to be a good idea when you pass me the ball in the position that, um, I'm in, to take the ball to the goal. What I need to do is move somewhere else, so that when you pass me the ball, I'll be in a better position for you... For me to score and take the ball to the goal, or I could then pass the ball back to you. I'll go ahead and repeat this because that was a little confusing, so let's try this. So I'm going to move diagonally to shift my position, [2][3]and now[4] I have the ball. So after I have checked, I need to either decide if I will pass the ball back to you or if I will turn around the opponent and dribble it to the goal. Right now, since I'm on the very side of the field, I don't think it's an advantage for me to take the ball right to the goal, because the opponent could then block me and off to the side. So then I'm going to pass it back to you.[5] [6][7]Then you would be able to go around the opponent and go straight to the goal. That is why checking is advantageous, so that the opponent will be have to considering both of our positions, and we can then move the ball around to which position is better for us to score the goal.",
